<title>CROATIA: Croatia to export 100,000 T maize - agency.</title>
<headline>Croatia to export 100,000 T maize - agency.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Croatia will export some 100,000 tonnes of maize, the state news agency Hina quoted Agriculture Minister Matej Jankovic as saying on Monday.</p>
<p>It said Croatia had a surplus of between 300,000 and 400,000 tonnes of maize after an excellent 1996 harvest.</p>
<p>There were no figures for the total crop.</p>
<p>Jankovic was also quoted as saying the government would boost subsidies to farmers and fishermen by 10 percent to some 570 million kuna next year. -- Zagreb Newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
</text>
